  "freight_commentary": {
    "Dry Bulk Freight": "Capesize: The Capesize C5TC average improved by USD 9.9k/day closing the week at USD 54,791/ day. Trip from Continent to F.East is up by 12.7k/ day at USD 93,111/day, Transatlantic R/V is higher by 9k/day at USD 59,156/day, and Bolivar to Rotterdam is higher by 10.1k/day at USD 66,523/ day, while Transpacific R/V is increased by 13k/ day at USD 63,186/day. Trip from Tubarao to Rotterdam is increased by 9.1k/day at USD 45,091/day, China-Brazil R/V is higher by 5.1k/day at USD 50,970/day, and & trip from Saldanha Bay to Qinqdao is increased by 9.1k/day at USD 45,091/day.\n\nKamsarmax/Panamax: The Kamsarmax P5TC Timecharter average started the week at USD 20,834/day closing with an increase at USD 22,035/day. Trip from Skaw-Gib to F.East is im- proved by 1.1k/day at USD 31,393/day, Pacific R/ Vis up by 2.3k/day at USD 21,594/day, while Transatlantic R/V is increased at USD 21,350/day, and Singapore R/V via Atlantic is increased at USD 22,827/day.\n\nUltramax/Supramax: The Ultramax S11TC average closed the week about USD 0.4k/day higher than its opening at USD 21,177/day. The Supramax S10TC average closed the week about 0.4k/day higher than its opening at USD 19,143/day. The Baltic Su- pramax Asia S3TC average closed the week about 0.3k/day higher than previous week at USD 19,487/ day. N.China one Australian or Pacific R/V is im- proved by 0.5k/day at USD 19,469/day, USG to Skaw Passero is firmer by 1.5k/day at USD 31,984/ day. S.China trip via Indonesia to EC India is up by 0.5k/day at USD 23,158/day, trip from S.China via Indonesia to S.China pays USD 15,843/day, while Med/B.Sea to China/S.Korea is reduced at USD 23,368/day.\n\nHandysize: The Handysize HS7TC average closed the week improved by 0.3k/day at USD 16,199/day. Skaw-Passero trip to Boston-Galveston pays 0.5k/ day more at USD 11,221/day, Brazil to Cont. pays 0.9k/day more at USD 23,350/day, S.E. Asia trip to Spore/Japan 0.1k/day is firmer at USD 18,169/day, China/S.Korea/Japan round trip is increased by 0.1k/day at USD 17,281/day, and trip from U.S. Gulf to Cont. is increased by 0.9k/day at USD 15,814/ day, while N.China-S.Korea-Japan trip to S.E.Asia is increased by 0.1k/day at USD 17,819/day.",
    "Tanker Freight": "VLCC: average T/CE ended the week up by 42.8k/ day at USD 376,871/day. Middle East Gulf to China trip is up by 47.9k/day at USD 704,025/day. West Africa to China trip is up by 41.3k/day at USD 218,803/day and US Gulf to China trip is up by 39.2k/day at USD 207,784/day.\n\nSuezmax: average T/CE closed the week softer by 33.4k/day at USD 151,494/day. West Africa to Continent trip is up by 20.1k/day at USD 115,444/ day, Black Sea to Mediterranean is down by 86.9k/ day at USD 187,544/day, and Middle East Gulf to Med trip is improved by 8.7k/day at USD 334,555/ day, while trip from Guyana to ARA is improved by 16.2k/day at USD 112,512/day.\n\nAframax: average T/CE closed the week lower by 4.1k/day at USD 64,556/day. North Sea to Conti- nent trip is down by 11.3k/day at USD 93,061/day, Kuwait to Singapore is up by 3.1k/day at USD 97,600/day, while route from Caribbean to US Gulf trip is up by 7.3k/day at USD 49,200/day. Trip from South East Asia to East Coast Australia is down by 4.6k/day at USD 37,761/day & Cross Mediterranean trip is down by 25.4k/day at USD 59,552/day. US Gulf to UK-Continent is improved by 5.6k/day at USD 50,780/day and the East Coast Mexico to US Gulf trip is up by USD 8k/day at USD 48,582/day.\n\nProducts: The LR2 route (TC1) Middle East to Ja- pan is this week higher by 3.9k/day at USD 156,979/day. Trip from (TC15) Med to Far East has increased by 0.3k/day at USD 39,585/day and (TC20) AG to UK Continent is up by 8.7k/day at USD 125,860/day. The LR1 route (TC5) from Mid- dle East Gulf to Japan is up by 5.k/day at USD 121,959/day, while the (TC8) Middle East Gulf to UK-Continent is up by 8.7k/day at USD 125,860/ day and the (TC16) Amsterdam to Lome trip is im- proved at USD /day. The MR Atlantic Basket is in- creased by 5.5k/day at USD 27,229/day & the MR Pacific Basket earnings are improved by 1.6k/day at USD 44,311/day. The MR route from Rotterdam to New York (TC2) is firmer by 3.9k/day at USD 156,979/day, (TC6) Intermed (Algeria to Euro Med) earnings are firmer by5.k/day at USD 121,959/day, (TC14) US Gulf to Continent is down by 0.3k/day at USD 21,234/day, (TC18) US Gulf to Brazil earnings are higher by 1.3k/day at USD 64,207/day, (TC23) Amsterdam to Le Havre is higher by 4k/day at USD 39,604/day while Yeosu to Botany Bay (TC22) is softer by 3.5k/day at USD 5,729/day and ARA to West Africa (TC19) is up by 6.4k/day at USD 33,826/day."
